{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00541",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.69,
      "end_seconds": 13.31,
      "duration_seconds": 12.62,
      "text": "Sorry we're late. The bus took forever, and then I forgot my backpack at the bus stop, so we had to go back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.59,
      "end_seconds": 21.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "It's my fault, Doctor, I was still looking for the insurance card."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.77,
      "end_seconds": 35.69,
      "duration_seconds": 12.92,
      "text": "Not a problem at all, you're here now. Hi there, buddy. So this is your asthma check-up. Tell me how you've been breathing lately."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.54,
      "end_seconds": 44.96,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "Um, okay, I guess. Sometimes my chest feels kinda squeezy when I run around at recess."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.81,
      "end_seconds": 52.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Squeezy, I like that description. Is it like someone's hugging your chest too tight?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.85,
      "end_seconds": 62.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "Yeah, like that. And then I have to stop and sit down for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.36,
      "end_seconds": 71.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "That's helpful. How long does the squeezy feeling last when you sit down?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.29,
      "end_seconds": 81.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Not long. Like, a few minutes? Then it goes away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.49,
      "end_seconds": 90.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Okay. And what about at night? Do you ever cough when you're in bed?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.66,
      "end_seconds": 99.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.09,
      "text": "Sometimes I cough at night and it wakes me up. Only a little, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 100.94,
      "end_seconds": 115.15,
      "duration_seconds": 14.21,
      "text": "It's more than a little, honey. I hear him coughing through the wall at least three nights a week, and some nights it goes on for a long time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.15,
      "end_seconds": 121.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "How long has the night cough been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 122.51,
      "end_seconds": 126.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "About one month, since the weather turned cold."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 129.35,
      "end_seconds": 135.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "[from the hallway] He was wheezing a lot at the game on Saturday!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.19,
      "end_seconds": 153.15,
      "duration_seconds": 14.96,
      "text": "Sorry, I didn't catch who that was. But that's a good point to follow up on. Buddy, do you remember a whistling sound when you breathed at the game?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.53,
      "end_seconds": 163.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "Kind of. Like a whistly sound when I breathe out. Not all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.98,
      "end_seconds": 170.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "Alright. Now, has he had any fever recently, or been sick with a cold?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 171.72,
      "end_seconds": 179.82,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "No fever. He had a little sniffle a couple of weeks ago, but nothing since then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.9,
      "end_seconds": 188.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "And when he coughs, does he bring up any yellow or green phlegm?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.89,
      "end_seconds": 194.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "No, nothing comes up. It's just a dry cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.05,
      "end_seconds": 202.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Good. Let's talk about his medicines. Can you tell me what he takes and how?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 204.37,
      "end_seconds": 215.75,
      "duration_seconds": 11.38,
      "text": "Sure. There's the fluticasone, that's the daily inhaler. He's supposed to take it twice a day, morning and night, with the spacer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.29,
      "end_seconds": 222.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "I take it every day. I never forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 224.78,
      "end_seconds": 236.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.92,
      "text": "Buddy, I'm sorry, but he skips the morning one a lot. We're always rushing for the bus. Nights I make sure of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.0,
      "end_seconds": 246.68,
      "duration_seconds": 8.68,
      "text": "I appreciate you both being honest. We'll come back to that. What else is he using?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 249.31,
      "end_seconds": 263.7,
      "duration_seconds": 14.39,
      "text": "The albuterol, for when he gets wheezy. He takes it when he needs it, and I'd say maybe twice a week. And the montelukast, 5 mg chewable, at bedtime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.06,
      "end_seconds": 273.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "Alright. Any other health problems, besides the asthma? I see eczema in his chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 275.39,
      "end_seconds": 280.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Yeah, he still gets dry patches in the elbow creases."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.4,
      "end_seconds": 285.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Okay. And any surgeries in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 286.94,
      "end_seconds": 293.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "His mom told me he had his tonsils out when he was five."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.94,
      "end_seconds": 304.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.24,
      "text": "Good to know. Does anyone in the family have asthma, that you know of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 305.8,
      "end_seconds": 308.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "His dad has asthma too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.75,
      "end_seconds": 322.1,
      "duration_seconds": 11.35,
      "text": "That fits the pattern, asthma often runs in families. Buddy, what do you like to do for fun, besides recess?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.06,
      "end_seconds": 331.29,
      "duration_seconds": 8.23,
      "text": "I play soccer on Saturdays. I'm a goalie, so I don't run that much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.46,
      "end_seconds": 337.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Let me get his numbers now. Sit tight, buddy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.7,
      "end_seconds": 356.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.06,
      "text": "Temperature is 36.9 degrees Celsius, heart rate is 92 beats per minute, and breathing rate is 20 breaths per minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.52,
      "end_seconds": 370.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Oxygen saturation is 98 percent, and he weighs 72 pounds today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 372.6,
      "end_seconds": 375.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Is that good, Doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.8,
      "end_seconds": 389.84,
      "duration_seconds": 13.04,
      "text": "The numbers are all in a comfortable range, so nothing to worry about there. Now, how about his tummy and bowels, any problems there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 392.01,
      "end_seconds": 394.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "No, his stomach is fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 396.88,
      "end_seconds": 415.25,
      "duration_seconds": 18.37,
      "text": "Great. Let me explain what I think is going on. With the squeezy chest on running, the night cough several nights a week, and the wheeze at the game, it sounds like his asthma isn't fully controlled right now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 417.54,
      "end_seconds": 421.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Is that because he misses the morning inhaler?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.19,
      "end_seconds": 434.0,
      "duration_seconds": 9.81,
      "text": "Very likely. The daily inhaler calms the lining of the airways, but only if it's used every day, like brushing teeth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.22,
      "end_seconds": 439.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "So I have to do it every morning?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.34,
      "end_seconds": 454.79,
      "duration_seconds": 12.45,
      "text": "Yes, and here's a trick: keep the inhaler right next to your toothbrush, and take your puffs before you brush. Then rinse your mouth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 457.35,
      "end_seconds": 463.37,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "That I can do. I'll put it right next to the toothbrush tonight."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 464.34,
      "end_seconds": 469.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Wonderful. And the albuterol, buddy: take it before soccer, every Saturday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 472.37,
      "end_seconds": 482.1,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "I'm not changing his medicines today, since I'd like to see first how he does when the daily inhaler is taken properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 483.19,
      "end_seconds": 492.71,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "Let's see him again in six weeks, and we'll check how the cough and the squeezy chest are doing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 495.14,
      "end_seconds": 503.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.92,
      "text": "I'll book it at the front desk. And if he gets bad before then?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 504.12,
      "end_seconds": 517.35,
      "duration_seconds": 13.23,
      "text": "If he needs the albuterol more than usual, or he's struggling to breathe, call us right away or go to the emergency room."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 519.21,
      "end_seconds": 524.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "Thank you so much, Doctor. Come on, let's get you a snack."
    }
  ]
}
